 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 532560,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the area of the shaded region in the given figure.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/cfcae5b3e67adef3.png\" alt=\"A square is circumscribed about a circle. The diameter of the circle is marked 10 centimeters. Each side of the square measures 10 centimeters. The region outside the circle is shaded.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Step 1: Find the area of the square.</p>\n<p>The area of a square with side <i>s</i> is <span data-math=\"A = {s^2}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = {s^2} = {\\left( {10{\\text{ cm}}} \\right)^2} = 100{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Find the area of the circle.</p>\n<p>The area of a circle with radius <i>r</i> is <span data-math=\"A = \\pi {r^2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"A = \\pi {r^2} = \\pi {\\left( {{\\text{5 cm}}} \\right)^2} = 25\\pi {\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span> (Keeping this exact makes your final answer more accurate.)</p>\n<p>Step 3: Subtract the area of the circle from the area of the square.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"100{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} - 25\\pi {\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2} = 21.46{\\text{ c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\"></span></p>\n<p>The shaded area is approximately 21.46 square centimeters.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"21.46\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}\">21.46\\,{\\text{c}}{{\\text{m}}^2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
